            <div xml:id="d775">

                <pb facs="0927" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.90 j 2/–</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Aden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Park</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Aden</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1927-03-15"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 15, 1927</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received
                        April 6.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 207</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform the Department
                    that the Imam of Yemen, Mohamed Yehia bin Mohamed, Hamid-ud-Din, Amir Al
                    Moumenin, Mutawakkil Al Allah, has forwarded to this Consulate, through the
                    unofficial intermediary of the Honorable Charles R. Crane, former American
                    Minister to China, who recently visited Sanaa in a personal capacity, a rough
                    draft in Arabic of a treaty of friendship and commerce which the Imam verbally
                    stated he would like to serve as the nucleus of an agreement. An English
                    translation of the Imam’s tentative draft is appended hereto for the
                    Department’s information and possible consideration for future action.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Loder Park</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d775-a1.xml" xpointer="d775-a1"/>
            </div>
